From 604c14f0e92d0f8264a3fc9576c68e10080859fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:13:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: block device (wasmblk) backed by the host's storage

/dev/wda: blk-mq, one request in flight, described in a shared slot
(op, sector, memory segments) that the host's disk worker serves before
raising WASM_IRQ_BLOCK.  The driver waits at probe for the host to open
the store and publish the capacity.  defconfig: BLOCK, ext4 (also for
ext2), overlayfs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/wasm/configs/wasm_defconfig |   6 +-
 arch/wasm/drivers/Kconfig        |   7 ++
 arch/wasm/drivers/Makefile       |   1 +
 arch/wasm/drivers/wasmblk.c      | 207 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 220 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/wasm/drivers/wasmblk.c

